Analyzing Loop Execution
First determine the order of the loop body, then multiply it 
by the number of times the loop will execute
Example:
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
// Sequence of statements that execute in O(1)
}
The statements in loop body execute in constant time = 𝑂(1)
The number of loop iterations is equal to n
Therefore, the time complexity of the loop is 𝑂(𝑛)

Analyzing Loop Execution
Consider the following loop:
while (count < n) {
count = count * 2;
// Sequence of statements that execute in O(1)
}
The statements in loop body execute in constant time = 𝑂(1)
The number of loop iterations = log2 𝑛
Therefore, the time complexity of the loop is 𝑂(log2 𝑛)

