Analyzing Nested Loop Execution
When loops are nested, we multiply the complexity of the 
outer loop by the complexity of the inner loop
Consider the following nested loops:
for (int i=0; i < n; i++)
for (int j=0; j < n; j++) {
// Sequence of statements that execute in O(1)
}
Both the inner and outer loops have complexity of 𝑂(𝑛)
The overall time complexity of the nested loops is 𝑂(𝑛2)

