// Print the sum of numbers from 1 to count
public void printsum(int count) {
  int sum = 0;
  for (int i=1; i <= count; i++) sum += i;
  System.out.println("sum = " + sum);
}

slides.raw_text:
Analyzing Method Calls
// Print the sum of numbers from 1 to count
public void printsum(int count) {
int sum = 0;
for (int i=1; i <= count; i++) sum += i;
System.out.println("sum = " + sum);
}
There is a loop inside printsum that repeats count times. 
The method is called n times with count = 1, 2, …, n.
The for loop inside printsum is executed 1 + 2 + ⋯+ 𝑛=
𝑛×(𝑛+1)
iterations and has a time complexity = 𝑂(𝑛2)

