// Print the sum of numbers from 1 to count
public void printsum(int count) {
int sum = count*(count+1)/2;
System.out.println("sum = " + sum);
}
The time complexity of the improved printsum is 𝑂(1)
The time complexity of the for loop that calls the method 
printsum 𝑛times is 𝑂(𝑛).

Exercise
Determine the growth function 𝑡(𝑛) and order of execution 
time in Big-O notation of the following nested loops:
for (int i=0; i<n; i++)
for (int j=0; j<n; j += 2)
System.out.println(i + ", " + j);
Solution: The outer for loop is repeated 𝑛times. The inner 
for loop is repeated 𝑛/2 times.
The growth function 𝑡(𝑛) = 𝑛× 𝑛/2 = 𝑛2/2
The order of execution time is 𝑂(𝑛2)

